{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And Benjamin.</b> We translate it וּדְבָרוּ יָת בִּנְיָמִין — because the taking of silver and the taking of a person are not equal in Aramaic. For an object taken by hand, we translate וּנְסִיב; but for something taken through the conduct of words, we translate וּדְבַר."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 43, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:03:19.623940335Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}